WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.180
Marvel's Defenders unites its four street-level
heroes, Daredevil, Jessica Jones, Luke Cage

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.480
and Iron Fist against the forces of The Hand
and, like any good Marvel production, it's

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:14.160
got plenty of hidden easter eggs, cameos,
call-backs and in-jokes.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.640
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm revealing some of the best easter

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.519
eggs, moments and connections in The Defenders.

00:00:21.519 --> 00:00:26.439
My giveaway for a Defenders or Punisher Funko
Pop is also running on this video, so subscribe

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:28.539
and keep watching to find out how to win.

00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:32.710
And, just before I delve in, be aware I will
be discussing spoilers.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.680
Luke Cage has certainly earned a reputation
with the ladies in these Netflix shows, starting

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.500
with Jessica Jones in the first season of
her series.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.390
After they broke up, Luke moved to Harlem
where his adventures on his own show gave

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:48.390
life to a series of Luke Cage coffee memes
which picked up on his and other characters'

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:51.050
use of the word coffee as a euphemism for
sex.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:55.420
And The Defenders includes a clever wink to
this in-joke via the Single Origin Coffee

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.600
posters you can spot behind Luke when he meets
with Misty Knight.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.500
In the Luke Cage series, after Misty asked
him out for coffee and he confessed he didn't

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.030
like it, they ended up sleeping together.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:10.340
That coffee joke continues in another Defenders
episode with a coffee poster placed behind

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:14.600
Luke while he talks to Claire Temple, who
he'd previously asked out for coffee in Luke

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.320
Cage, but she refused saying she wasn't going
to sleep with him.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.600
And, intriguingly, in the final episode of
The Defenders, Jessica says to Luke that 'Maybe

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.469
we'll grab a coffee sometime or something',
so perhaps we'll see Luke and Jessica back

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:30.479
together at some point in the future.

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:33.700
And during that conversation between Luke
and Claire, she gives him the name of the

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:36.310
bar where he then goes to interrogate Turk.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:40.590
The bar's name, "Trouble In A Pair Of Dice",
previously appeared in an old New York Bulletin

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:45.420
newspaper that Karen Page was sifting through
in Daredevil Season 2.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.409
During Jessica Jones's investigations at the
records office, there's a nod to the Hand

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:53.259
villain Nobu, who was rumoured to have lived
three lifetimes back in the second season

00:01:53.259 --> 00:01:54.289
of Daredevil.

00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:58.479
One of the files Jessica stumbles across is
for a corporation called Yoshioka, which is

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:03.869
Nobu's surname, and in the comics it was Kagenobu
Yoshioka who founded the villainous organisation,

00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:05.500
the Hand.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.600
And in other hand-related matters, we all
know Marvel loved to chop off hands and arms

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:14.220
in its Phase 2 movies as an homage to Star
Wars, but, like other Marvel Netflix shows

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:20.210
before it, Defenders includes its own limb-losing
WTF moment when Stick chops off his own hand

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.489
to escape Alexandra's clutches.

00:02:22.489 --> 00:02:26.760
You could say there's a bit of ironic symbolism
here in that he has to cut off his own hand

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:29.120
to escape the villainous group the Hand.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.000
Interestingly also, this moment is probably
a call-back to the time Stick sliced off a

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.290
Hand villain's hand in the first season of
Daredevil.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:40.760
Speaking of losing limbs, remember how in
season 1 of Luke Cage, Misty Knight injured

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.610
her arm during the hostage siege at Harlem's
Paradise?

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:48.329
Well, that was a hint to the comics where
her character loses an arm during a bomb attack.

00:02:48.329 --> 00:02:53.000
But season 1 of The Defenders took that hint
and made it reality when Misty's arm was lopped

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.090
off at Midland Circle while she was battling
the Hand alongside Colleen Wing.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:01.689
Now, comic-book Misty was given a bionic arm
by Tony Stark, and it seems she's being set

00:03:01.689 --> 00:03:03.780
up for something similar on the show too.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:07.819
However, I'm guessing it will be a different
billionaire who'll be responsible for giving

00:03:07.819 --> 00:03:11.129
Misty a super-powered limb in the Defenders-verse.

00:03:11.129 --> 00:03:14.900
Given the fact that, at the end of the season,
she's shown recuperating at a state-of-the-art

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:19.469
hospital owned by rich boy Danny Rand, I think
Misty will have Danny and his connections,

00:03:19.469 --> 00:03:23.500
as Colleen refers to them, to thank for her
new bionic arm.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:27.610
The patient care board in Misty's hospital
room also includes a couple of hidden Marvel

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:28.879
easter eggs.

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:33.409
First is the name L Carter, short for Linda
Carter, a nurse in the comics who specialised

00:03:33.409 --> 00:03:37.690
in taking care of injured superheroes and
took on the alias of "Night Nurse".

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:42.349
Also listed is Dr E Wirtham, an easter egg
to Elias Wirtham, a doctor in the comics who

00:03:42.349 --> 00:03:45.650
ended up becoming a vigilante and anti-hero
called Cardiac.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:50.549
I wonder whether we'll see Wirtham turn up
as the character who fits Misty's new bionic

00:03:50.549 --> 00:03:54.520
arm, or if this is just an easter egg, plain
and simple.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.270
On the subject of Misty, I've gotta say I
loved seeing her hand Colleen her katana at

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:02.709
the police station, in a nice bit of foreshadowing
of their fight scene on the show and also

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.390
of their partnership in the comics.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:08.390
Of course, it was pretty cool seeing Misty
and Colleen battle alongside each other in

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:12.739
the series, in a hat tip to their comic-book
team-up as the 'Daughters of the Dragon'.

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:18.370
Plus, Colleen's white top and Misty's reddy-orange
one echo their costumes in the comic books.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:22.440
And as Misty's due to appear in season 2 of
Iron Fist, it's fair to say we'll be seeing

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.940
a lot more of her and Colleen together!

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:28.680
Since Simone Missick and Jessica Henwick are
both excellent in their respective roles,

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.350
this can only be a good thing!

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:35.540
Stan Lee makes a cameo in the show with a
similar NYPD picture to ones we've seen in

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.190
many of his other Marvel Netflix cameos.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:42.710
This particular poster adds a nice touch though
with the line "Not all heroes wear capes",

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:47.150
a nod to the show's street-level heroes, obviously,
none of whom wear capes.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:52.120
And the show really gets into its stride in
the third episode when it busts out an epic

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:58.139
corridor scene after all four heroes finally
team up to take on the Hand at Midland Circle.

00:04:58.139 --> 00:05:02.560
Corridor fight scenes are a staple of Marvel's
Netflix shows and this one has a pretty spectacular

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:07.349
ending with Iron Fist using his punch to shatter
Elektra's blade.

00:05:07.349 --> 00:05:11.319
The show tips its hat in a couple of ways
to the mythical dragon Danny Rand had to defeat

00:05:11.319 --> 00:05:13.210
in order to become the Iron Fist.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:16.979
There's the name of the restaurant, the "Royal
Dragon", where the Defenders retreat to after

00:05:16.979 --> 00:05:19.289
their first Midland Circle battle.

00:05:19.289 --> 00:05:23.210
And Iron Fist's origins are also referenced
in several jokes between Claire, Colleen,

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:27.360
Luke, and Danny about how crazy all his talk
about dragons is.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.600
By the way, it's great to see how the cinematography
and production design from all the solo shows

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.940
really come together in The Defenders.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:38.199
For example, just look at how the colours
associated with Daredevil, Jessica Jones,

00:05:38.199 --> 00:05:41.840
Luke Cage, and Iron Fist are reflected in
the sign for the Royal Dragon restaurant,

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.140
where the Defenders team up, as well as in
the lighting and fixtures and fittings inside

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.140
the restaurant.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:51.830
There are also a few cool shout-outs to Game
of Thrones, which is fitting as both Finn

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:55.550
Jones and Jessica Henwick starred in the HBO
fantasy series.

00:05:55.550 --> 00:06:00.010
Of course, it's a nice coincidence that there's
lots of talk of dragons in both shows, even

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:04.260
if the Marvel shows don't have the budget
to put them on screen in the way that Thrones

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.260
does.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.571
More intriguingly, though, is the appearance
in The Defenders of two lines that have found

00:06:08.571 --> 00:06:13.110
their way into everyday language thanks to
their popularity in Game of Thrones.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:17.490
During the Midland Circle battle, when Bakuto
is about to bring his sword down on Daredevil,

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:22.629
Colleen Wing blocks Bakuto with her own sword,
and, as she does so, she says the line 'Not

00:06:22.629 --> 00:06:27.990
Today', which is Syrio Forel's classic retort
to the god of Death in Game of Thrones.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:33.050
And in episode 8, Elektra says to Matt, 'You
know nothing', something Ygritte often used

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:35.490
to tell Jon Snow on Game of Thrones.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:40.560
There's a cool Spider-Man easter egg via the
lyrics of the Wu-Tang Clan song "Protect Ya

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:44.440
Neck" which plays during the final fight scene
and includes the line "Swingin' through your

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:47.419
town like your neighborhood Spider-Man".

00:06:47.419 --> 00:06:51.909
At the end of the season, this scene of Matt
Murdoch bandaged in bed, a beside-table and

00:06:51.909 --> 00:06:56.909
window either side of him, a cross above him,
and a nun sitting by his side, strongly evokes

00:06:56.909 --> 00:06:59.860
this image from Daredevil issue 230.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:04.410
The fact the show chose to include that huge
visual easter egg has potentially massive

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:08.979
consequences for events in the next season
of Daredevil, and I'll talk in lots more detail

00:07:08.979 --> 00:07:13.720
about that in my upcoming video on what we
can expect in Daredevil Season 3.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:18.330
And the final Defenders episode also includes
a post-credits teaser for the new Punisher

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:21.250
series with lots of Frank Castle easter eggs
and references.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:25.320
I've made a full video breakdown of that which
you can watch by tapping the top-right of

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:29.710
the screen here, and there's also a link to
that in the video description and at the end

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:31.120
of this video.

